"A habit log split across two Prose files. Run it with: node bin/prose.js examples/habits.prose --run"

use longest_streak, note_length, summary from "./habit_rules.prose"

"A check-in is a day number and an optional note."
function check_in takes day, note
    entry is object
        day is day
        note is note
    return entry

"Each call takes its own two arguments, so commas between calls separate the check-ins."
log is new Map
log:set with "Stretch", (check_in 1, "stiff", check_in 2, unset, check_in 3, "loose", check_in 5, unset)
log:set with "Read", (check_in 1, unset, check_in 2, "two chapters", check_in 3, unset, check_in 4, unset, check_in 5, unset)
log:set with "Walk", (check_in 4, unset,)

"for each takes Map entries apart. Imported functions need no with: they keep their argument counts."
for each name, entries in log
    days is entries:map with function takes entry return entry:day
    print summary with name, (longest_streak days)
    noted is entries:filter with function takes entry return note_length entry > 0
    if length noted > 0
        notes is noted:map with function takes entry return entry:note
        print "  notes: " + (notes:join with "; ")

"summary with all three arguments, using its marker."
print summary "Read", (longest_streak (5, 6, 7)), "*"

"maybe also covers methods: a habit with no check-ins has no list to call map on."
swim is log:get with "Swim"
swim_days is maybe swim:map with function takes entry return entry:day
print "Swim days: " + (swim_days otherwise "none yet")

"Arithmetic right after with arguments must say what it means, so this uses parentheses."
read_days is (log:get with "Read"):map with function takes entry return entry:day
print "Day 3 is check-in number " + ((read_days:indexOf with 3) + 1)
